---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Robot Design and Portfolio">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section>
        <div class="overlay">
            <h1>Our 2025-2026 Robot — Bing Bong</h1>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FINAL SOLUTION -->
    <section class="angled">
        <h2>Final Solution</h2>

        <img
            src="/robottransparent.png"
            width="40%"
            alt="Picture of the 2025-2026 robot, Bing Bong"
        />

        <p>
            Bing Bong is our FTC DECODE competition robot. It is almost entirely
            3D‑printed and designed with reliability, consistency, and efficient
            game‑play strategy at its core.
        </p>
    </section>

    <!-- DRIVE TRAIN -->
    <section class="angled">
        <h2>Drive Train</h2>

        <img
            src="/bingbong/drivecad.png"
            alt="Picture of the drivetrain CAD for Bing Bong"
            width="40%"
        />

        <p>
            It features a mecanum drive train for omnidirectional movement. In
            addition, we utilize a pinpoint odometry system that allows us to
            create highly consistent autonomous routines.
        </p>
    </section>

    <!-- HOPPER / OUTTAKE -->
    <section class="angled">
        <h2>Hopper & Outtake</h2>

        <div
            style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;"
        >
            <img
                src="/bingbong/shooterfinal.png"
                width="30%"
                alt="Picture of the hopper/shooter for Bing Bong in real life"
            />
            <img
                src="/bingbong/shootercad.png"
                width="30%"
                alt="Picture of the hopper/shooter for Bing Bong in CAD"
            />
        </div>

        <p>
            We utilized a gravity‑fed hopper and a double flywheel shooter for
            accurate and consistent scoring throughout the season.
        </p>

        <br />

        <p>
            Throughout the season, the robot underwent continuous iterations to
            improve performance, reduce jams, better support our electrical
            system, and maximize consistency.
        </p>
    </section>

    <!-- WIRING -->
    <section class="angled">
        <h2>Electrical System & Wiring</h2>

        <img
            src="/bingbong/wiring.png"
            width="30%"
            alt="Image of Bing Bong's wiring"
        />

        <p>
            After our first competition, we learned a great deal about wire
            management. We fixed our mistakes and came back stronger for the
            Greenwood competition, where we were the second member of the
            winning alliance.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>
